three predecessor features for each leg's fit against documented mileage. The Helena-Butte third is drawn on an abandoned grade; the rest is live or disused BNSF track on the original alignment.", "segments": [{"start": 1890, "end": 1907, "headway_min": 480, "note": "Hill transferred the Montana Central and the Manitoba road to the Great Northern on Feb 1 1890, and from then on the Havre-Great Falls-Helena-Butte line was Great Northern property, worked as the railway's branch off its own transcontinental main at Havre. The Montana Central kept a paper existence until 1907. Frequency estimated, unsourced", "sources": ["Segment-level: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montana_Central_Railway (ownership transferred to the Great Northern Feb 1 1890; the Montana Central ceased to exist when absorbed into the Great Northern in 1907). Service pattern: https://storyofbutte.org/items/show/3527 (Great Northern Passenger Station, Butte) (the Butte station \"served the railway's passenger trains that connected Havre on the transcontinental line to Great Falls, Helena, and Butte\"). Headway is an estimate.", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montana_Central_Railway", "https://storyofbutte.org/items/show/3527 (Great Northern Passenger Station, Butte)"]}, {"start": 1907, "end": 1950, "headway_min": 720, "note": "The Montana Central was dissolved into the Great Northern outright in 1907, and Butte got a new Great Northern passenger station on Feb 1 1914. Through the first half of the century this was the Great Northern's Montana north-south passenger route, feeding the transcontinental trains at Havre. Frequency estimated, unsourced", "sources": ["Segment-level (dates only): https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montana_Central_Railway (Montana Central absorbed into the Great Northern, 1907); https://storyofbutte.org/items/show/3527 (Great Northern Passenger Station, Butte) (Butte passenger station opened Feb 1 1914). The 1950 boundary is editorial, not a sourced event, and the headway is an estimate.", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montana_Central_Railway", "https://storyofbutte.org/items/show/3527 (Great Northern Passenger Station, Butte)"]}, {"start": 1950, "end": 1961, "headway_min": 1440, "note": "By the end the whole run was worked by a single self-propelled railcar, nicknamed the galloping goose. Great Northern passenger service to Butte ended on Sep 6 1961 -- a decade before Amtrak, and the reason no passenger train has served Great Falls since. Frequency estimated, unsourced", "sources": ["Segment-level: https://storyofbutte.org/items/show/3527 (Great Northern Passenger Station, Butte) (\"Great Northern's last scheduled passenger train service was a single self-propelled rail car, nicknamed the 'galloping goose'\" and \"Service to Butte ended on September 6, 1961\"). The 1950 start of this segment is editorial; the headway is an estimate.", "https://storyofbutte.org/items/show/3527 (Great Northern Passenger Station, Butte)"]}]}, "geometry": {"type": "LineString", "coordinates": [[-109.67714, 48.55464], [-109.69893, 48.55676], [-109.72083, 48.56428], [-109.72533, 48.56474], [-109.72957, 48.5634], [-109.7386, 48.55704], [-109.74134, 48.55594], [-109.76186, 48.55643], [-109.76817, 48.55536], [-109.78695, 48.5453], [-109.78853, 48.54361], [-109.78955, 48.54077], [-109.78855, 48.52766], [-109.78985, 48.52391], [-109.79326, 48.52158], [-109.80875, 48.51514], [-109.81132, 48.51347], [-109.82264, 48.49279], [-109.93398, 48.3821], [-109.96088, 48.3583], [-110.01791, 48.31423], [-110.04798, 48.25893], [-110.06728, 48.23144], [-110.08352, 48.20601], [-110.09314, 48.19434], [-110.21591, 48.1041], [-110.22389, 48.09677], [-110.24197, 48.07496], [-110.24133, 48.06808], [-110.24336, 48.06263], [-110.24318, 48.0606], [-110.24212, 48.05875], [-110.23727, 48.05466], [-110.23559, 48.05237], [-110.23413, 48.04492], [-110.23276, 48.04189], [-110.23304, 48.03866], [-110.23481, 48.03507], [-110.24177, 48.03211], [-110.24824, 48.02602], [-110.24938, 48.02328], [-110.2513